{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 61, :comments ["<b>And they rode.</b> On the camels that the servant brought." "<b>וַיֵלַך.</b> Open [with patach]. If it is the end of a verse, it is not given kamatz, because at the beginning it had a small patach, and it cannot rise two degrees. And so too every ויֹאמַר." "The sense of \"the servant took Rebekah and went\" — he was walking along with Rebekah and did not notice until Isaac came."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra refers to the kamatz gadol conversion that normally occurs at the end of a verse for words with patach in the open syllable; he explains why וַיֵלַך does not receive it here."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:41.505352484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}